/**
 * Symbol path registry for `ServiceSign` (Icelandic class E service signs).
 * Each entry is a list of glyph paths extracted from the matching reference
 * sign artwork (`Iceland_road_sign_<code>.svg` on Wikimedia Commons), already
 * resolved to the shared coordinate space used by `serviceSignShape.ts`
 * (`SERVICE_SIGN_VIEW_BOX`) -- no extra `<G transform>` is needed for these
 * paths, since every reference sign uses the same board/frame/icon-slot
 * layout and coordinates were normalised while extracting.
 *
 * Most symbols are a single colour and use plain `d` strings, recoloured via
 * `ServiceSign`'s `iconColour` prop (same convention as `WarningSign` and
 * `ProhibitorySign`). A symbol part that must always render in a fixed
 * colour regardless of `iconColour` uses the `{ d, colour }` form --
 * `PoliceStation` is the only symbol with a fixed-colour accent (a yellow
 * star/badge behind the black crest details).
 *
 * A symbol with multiple disjoint subpaths of the same colour (e.g.
 * `Information`'s dot + body, `PublicLavatory`'s "W" + "C") has all of its
 * subpaths concatenated into a single `d` string, one `Path` per colour.
 * IMPORTANT: every subpath's leading moveto is forced to uppercase `M`
 * (absolute) here -- per the SVG spec, only the very first moveto of an
 * entire `d` string gets the "lowercase-but-treated-as-absolute" special
 * case; every subsequent lowercase `m` inside a joined string would
 * otherwise be interpreted as a *relative* moveto (relative to the previous
 * subpath's last point), silently shifting every subpath after the first
 * one out of place. Keep using `M` for any new multi-subpath colour group
 * added here.
 *
 * `RadioStation` has no icon paths -- the reference artwork bakes in the
 * station name and FM frequency as vector text outlines rather than a
 * pictogram, so `ServiceSign` renders that sign as two lines of free text
 * (`firstLineText` / `secondLineText`) instead, each independently scaled to
 * fill the width of the white icon slot.
 *
 * `Car`, `Snowmobile`, `Bike` and `Boat` are vehicle-only icons (the "key"
 * glyph that appears above them in the reference "rental" signs -
 * E03.41/E07.61/E07.63/E07.64 - is extracted once as
 * `SERVICE_SIGN_RENTAL_KEY_PATH` and drawn separately by `ServiceSign`
 * whenever its `rental` prop is true, fit-scaled against whichever symbol is
 * selected via `SERVICE_SIGN_SYMBOL_BBOX`).
 */
